    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2782dedb-fc86-58f0-ae37-6e597d762c30",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4z &=-9 \\\\ y+z &=-5 \\\\ z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_{2}:=R_{2}-R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 4 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}-4R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$",
