    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a9833e61-39d5-5aa6-ad6e-23679fbb685a",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4z &=9 \\\\ y-3z &=0 \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_{2}:=R_{2}+3R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}-4R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$",
