      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y+5z &=-7 \\\\ y &=7 \\\\ z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -4 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}-5R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -4 & 0 & -27 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}+4R_{2},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$",
