      ":question/id": "cfa56d3b-8643-5e85-b906-1cb2df5375d0",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+3z &=4 \\\\ y &=2 \\\\ z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}-3R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}+3R_{2},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2 \\\\ y &=2 \\\\ z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=-2$, $y=2$, and $z=4$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -2,2,4\\rangle$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
